│ patch_description        │ Replace the degenerate all-zero construction with a deterministic maximin optimization    │
│                          │ specialized to the equilateral-triangle Heilbronn problem. Three vertices are fixed at    │
│                          │ the boundary corners, while the remaining eight points are globally searched in           │
│                          │ barycentric coordinates, which guarantees feasibility without penalty terms. The          │
│                          │ objective evaluates all 165 triples using normalized area (the determinant in barycentric │
│                          │ coordinates equals triangle area divided by the containing triangle area). A fixed-seed   │
│                          │ differential-evolution phase provides robust global exploration, followed by SLSQP        │
│                          │ polishing with the orientation of every triple fixed locally. A deterministic fallback    │
│                          │ construction is retained if SciPy is unavailable or an optimizer failure occurs.          │
