│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ active_simplex_exchange                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation uses a deterministic active-constraint exchange search rather than    │
│                          │ returning a fixed lattice or relying on a generic optimizer. Points are represented in    │
│                          │ barycentric coordinates, which makes every proposed point automatically projectable into  │
│                          │ the equilateral triangle.                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The search fixes the three triangle vertices and optimizes the other eight points. At     │
│                          │ each iteration it identifies the movable point participating most heavily in the          │
│                          │ currently smallest triangles, generates a batch of local and occasional global            │
│                          │ barycentric proposals for that point, and retains the proposal maximizing a smooth        │
│                          │ lower-tail objective over all triangle areas. Several fixed-seed restarts and decreasing  │
│                          │ proposal scales provide deterministic coarse-to-fine exploration. The final returned      │
│                          │ arrangement is selected by its true minimum normalized triangle area.                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
