│ patch_name               │ deterministic_local_search                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the degenerate all-zero construction with a deterministic multi-start             │
│                          │ simulated-annealing search specialized for the 11-point Heilbronn problem. The three      │
│                          │ vertices are retained as useful extremal points, while the remaining eight points are     │
│                          │ repeatedly perturbed and projected back into the equilateral triangle. Each candidate is  │
│                          │ evaluated over all 165 triples using vectorized NumPy area computation.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The search uses a smoothed objective based on the smallest several triangle areas, rather │
│                          │ than only the current minimum. This gives the local search useful gradient-like           │
│                          │ information when several nearly active constraints compete. The best configuration is     │
│                          │ still selected strictly by its true minimum triangle area. Fixed RNG seeds make the       │
│                          │ returned arrangement reproducible, and all proposals are explicitly projected into the    │
│                          │ feasible triangular domain.                                                               │
