│ patch_description        │ The current search changes only one interior point per iteration. In high-quality         │
│                          │ Heilbronn configurations, several nearly active triangle constraints typically need       │
│                          │ coordinated motion of multiple points; single-point moves are often unable to cross the   │
│                          │ narrow feasibility barriers between combinatorial arrangements.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit retains the existing active-constraint-guided coordinate search and global      │
│                          │ replacements, but reserves several batch candidates for small simultaneous perturbations  │
│                          │ of all eight free barycentric points. The perturbation is intentionally smaller than the  │
│                          │ single-point scale, is projected back into the simplex for every point, and keeps the     │
│                          │ incumbent candidate unchanged. This adds basin-transition capability without increasing   │
│                          │ the number of area evaluations or materially increasing execution time.                   │
