╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ oriented_slsqp_polish                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Add a deterministic constrained maximin polishing stage after the stochastic search.  In  │
│                          │ simplex coordinates, signed determinants are normalized triangle areas.  The best         │
│                          │ simulated-annealing arrangement fixes a locally consistent orientation for every triple;  │
│                          │ maximizing an epigraph variable subject to those signed determinant constraints lets      │
│                          │ SLSQP directly equalize the active small-area triangles.  This is substantially more      │
│                          │ precise than random coordinate perturbations near the optimum, retains the three extremal │
│                          │ vertices, and falls back safely to the annealed result if SciPy is unavailable or the     │
│                          │ polish is not genuinely better.                                                           │
