│ patch_description        │ Add constraint-gradient-informed proposals to the local polishing phase. The current      │
│                          │ polish relies on isotropic random perturbations, which are inefficient near a maximin     │
│                          │ optimum because only a small set of near-minimum triangles controls the objective. For    │
│                          │ the currently smallest signed determinants, this edit computes their determinant          │
│                          │ gradients with respect to each free point, aggregates ascent directions, and evaluates    │
│                          │ projected steps at several magnitudes. Random trials remain available afterward for       │
│                          │ escaping nonsmooth local configurations, while the directed trials deliberately increase  │
│                          │ active triangle areas.                                                                    │
