│ patch_name               │ active_set_batch_refinement                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the purely greedy single-point hill climb with a batched active-set repair phase. │
│                          │ Heilbronn layouts are controlled by a small set of nearly minimum determinant             │
│                          │ constraints, so moving only one point at a time is often unable to escape coupled local   │
│                          │ optima. The new refinement repeatedly identifies the lowest-area triples, perturbs all    │
│                          │ points participating in those constraints jointly, and evaluates a vectorized batch of    │
│                          │ repair candidates. A small temporary lower-tail acceptance allowance lets the search      │
│                          │ traverse flat nonsmooth regions, while `elite` always preserves the best strict           │
│                          │ minimum-area arrangement encountered for the returned result.                             │
