│ patch_description        │ This replaces the coordinate-wise random walk with a population-based, vectorized         │
│                          │ JADE-style differential-evolution search in barycentric coordinates. The population       │
│                          │ maintains diverse complete layouts, uses current-to-elite mutations and archive           │
│                          │ differences to cross combinatorial barriers, and ranks candidates with an annealed        │
│                          │ soft-min lower-tail objective. The strongest layouts are then polished by solving the     │
│                          │ locally fixed-orientation maximin problem with SLSQP. This combines global layout-level   │
│                          │ exploration with an exact local maximin refinement while remaining deterministic and      │
│                          │ substantially reducing repeated single-point proposal overhead.                           │
