│ patch_name               │ active_triple_gradient_polish                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Augment the final local-search phase with constraint-gradient-informed proposals. The     │
│                          │ bottleneck in a Heilbronn layout is determined by a small set of active, near-minimal     │
│                          │ triples. For each iteration, this edit computes signed determinant gradients for the      │
│                          │ lowest-area triples, aggregates their normalized ascent directions for each movable       │
│                          │ point, and evaluates several projected directional steps alongside the existing random    │
│                          │ and coupled mutations.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This specifically targets increases in the limiting triangle areas rather than relying    │
│                          │ only on isotropic jitter. Retaining random candidates is important because active         │
│                          │ constraints may conflict and because occasional stochastic moves can escape a locally     │
│                          │ balanced but suboptimal contact pattern.                                                  │
