│ patch_name               │ archive_active_de                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses 34 long single-point annealing restarts (5350 iterations each),  │
│                          │ with initial scale 0.125, final scale 0.0075, and active-triangle-biased moves. This is   │
│                          │ robust but expensive and has limited coordinated population-level exploration.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new implementation uses normalized affine determinants directly, reducing repeated    │
│                          │ Cartesian conversion. It replaces most serial annealing with six deterministic            │
│                          │ differential-evolution islands using population size 120 and 340 generations. The first   │
│                          │ three islands use fresh structured/simplex populations; later islands use archive-seeded  │
│                          │ restarts, perturbing prior elite configurations while retaining some fresh samples.       │
│                          │ Selection prioritizes strict minimum determinant while using a small lower-tail score     │
│                          │ only for near ties. A final 760-round active-set batch polish uses 176 coordinated        │
│                          │ candidates per round, concentrating moves on points involved in the 18 smallest triangle  │
│                          │ constraints. This combines broad exploration, archive transfer, and targeted local        │
│                          │ repair.                                                                                   │
