│ patch_description        │ The current program uses 34 restarts × 5350 sequential single-candidate annealing moves,  │
│                          │ with initial scale 0.125, final scale 0.0075, and an exponentially decaying temperature.  │
│                          │ This is expensive because every proposal recomputes all 165 triangle areas separately,    │
│                          │ and late annealing can still accept a weaker strict bottleneck.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement uses vectorized differential-evolution islands: 3 islands of 144          │
│                          │ configurations for 420 generations, followed by a 520-round active-constraint batch       │
│                          │ polish with 128 proposals per round. All geometry is evaluated directly in affine simplex │
│                          │ coordinates, where determinant magnitude equals normalized triangle area. Early           │
│                          │ generations use a lower-tail score to balance several nearly active triangles; the final  │
│                          │ 45% switches to lexicographic selection dominated by the raw minimum area, preventing     │
│                          │ soft-tail improvements from sacrificing the true bottleneck. Active-set polishing         │
│                          │ perturbs points incident to the smallest 18 constraints, with decreasing scales from      │
│                          │ 0.020 to 0.00016.                                                                         │
