│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ lexicographic_slsqp_polish                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ This revision keeps the effective batched simplex search but improves the late-stage      │
│                          │ acceptance rule: during the final search phase, candidates are selected lexicographically │
│                          │ by the true minimum normalized triangle area first and by the lower-tail mean second.     │
│                          │ This prevents soft-min optimization from sacrificing the actual bottleneck triangle.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It also records several strong independent restart configurations and applies             │
│                          │ deterministic SLSQP maximin polishing with fixed local orientation signs. The polish      │
│                          │ directly maximizes the minimum normalized determinant subject to all triangle-area and    │
│                          │ simplex constraints, allowing the final configuration to balance active constraints more  │
│                          │ accurately than random local proposals alone. A cached result avoids repeated             │
│                          │ optimization work.                                                                        │
