│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ balanced_active_mutations                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace uniformly chosen single-point mutations and overly broad all-active-point joint   │
│                          │ perturbations with participation-weighted sampling from the active constraints. In        │
│                          │ maximin Heilbronn layouts, several different near-minimal triples usually compete, so     │
│                          │ repeatedly moving a uniformly random point wastes proposals, while moving every active    │
│                          │ point simultaneously destroys useful structure. Sampling from a tempered participation    │
│                          │ distribution focuses effort on points implicated in restrictive triangles but retains     │
│                          │ baseline exploration. Small coupled moves sample two to four independently implicated     │
│                          │ points, which better repairs coupled active constraints without making disruptive global  │
│                          │ moves.                                                                                    │
