│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ archive_restart_maximin                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The previous implementation used one large differential-evolution run (`popsize=24`,      │
│                          │ `maxiter=1400`) followed by one orientation-fixed SLSQP polish. This is expensive and can │
│                          │ converge to a weak order-type basin, as reflected by the approximately `0.02` minimum     │
│                          │ normalized area.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version uses two deterministic DE stages with a lower per-stage population           │
│                          │ (`popsize=18`) and moderate iteration budgets (`620` and `520`). The second stage is      │
│                          │ initialized from an archive around the best first-stage geometry, with                    │
│                          │ barycentric-variable perturbations at adaptive moderate scale (`0.11`) while retaining a  │
│                          │ fraction of fresh samples (`18%`). This preserves promising near-active triangle geometry │
│                          │ while still allowing changes in order type. Both archived candidates are then             │
│                          │ independently polished by SLSQP using fixed determinant orientations and maximin          │
│                          │ constraints. The best verified candidate is retained. Vectorized objective evaluation     │
│                          │ reduces Python overhead substantially.                                                    │
