│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ balanced_active_gradients                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Add several analytic ascent proposals derived from differently sized sets of the          │
│                          │ currently smallest determinant constraints. The existing search uses random coordinate    │
│                          │ and joint perturbations, but near a good Heilbronn configuration these can fail when      │
│                          │ several competing small triangles require coordinated yet partially conflicting repairs.  │
│                          │ The new candidates form four constraint-balanced gradient fields from the smallest 6, 12, │
│                          │ 24, and 40 triples. Within each field, triples involving overrepresented movable points   │
│                          │ are downweighted, reducing cancellation and preventing a single highly participating      │
│                          │ point from dominating the move. These deterministic directed proposals are inserted into  │
│                          │ otherwise unused candidate slots and preserve the incumbent candidate.                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
