│ patch_description        │ The optimum for the triangular Heilbronn problem can require free points on the boundary. │
│                          │ The current positive simplex margin excludes such arrangements and also moves any         │
│                          │ boundary solution returned by SLSQP back into the interior. Removing that artificial      │
│                          │ margin enlarges the feasible set without compromising validity.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, the directed stochastic phase explores several distinct orientation         │
│                          │ chambers, but only the single best raw layout is passed to the orientation-fixed SLSQP    │
│                          │ maximin polish. Keep each restart's best-ever layout in a small archive and polish the    │
│                          │ four strongest archive members. This is particularly valuable because SLSQP can           │
│                          │ substantially improve a chamber that is slightly weaker before polishing but has a more   │
│                          │ favorable active-constraint structure.                                                    │
