│ patch_name               │ add_oriented_maximin_polish                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Add a final constrained maximin refinement in barycentric coordinates. The stochastic     │
│                          │ coordinate search is useful for discovering an oriented-matroid cell, but its soft-tail   │
│                          │ selection does not accurately solve the nonsmooth maximum-minimum problem within that     │
│                          │ cell. Once a good state is found, fix each determinant’s observed sign and use SLSQP to   │
│                          │ maximize an explicit lower-bound variable subject to every signed determinant exceeding   │
│                          │ it and every free point remaining in the simplex. In a fixed sign cell these are smooth   │
│                          │ constraints, so this directly targets the normalized minimum area rather than the         │
│                          │ surrogate tail score. The refinement is protected by exception handling and only replaces │
│                          │ the search result after exact area verification.                                          │
